Title: "Introduction"
Id: "876a2473-4cc1-4281-a90c-268e0eda9952"

Text: "Mathlingua is a source language and toolchain for writing mathematical
knowledge in a structured form that remains readable to people. A document
combines formulation syntax—the expressions, forms, statements, and command
calls used for mathematics—with structural groups such as `Defines:`,
`Theorem:`, and `Text:`. The `mlg` tool parses, checks, formats, renders, and
exports collections of these documents.

This reference describes implemented behavior, not a proposed language. Start
with Getting Started for orientation. Use Formulation and Headers for notation,
Structural for document shapes, Type Checking for semantic rules, Rendering for
display behavior, and the mlg chapter for command-line operation. Current
Implementation Notes summarizes recent boundaries and removed spellings; the
Cheatsheet is a compact reminder after you know the concepts."
Id: "64f2bb6d-d297-48ee-8b3f-e93329ef8976"
